<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-09-18T11:42:02+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:42:02 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Whale Post-Mortem Behaviour: Study details mother’s vigil; scientists urge further observations]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134326041.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Off the Gold Coast of Australia, researchers captured a remarkable sight: a mother humpback whale exhibiting attentive behavior towards her stillborn calf resting on the ocean floor. This poignant spectacle lasted for several hours and marks the inaugural scientific documentation of such a phenomenon among humpback whales, shedding light on the profound maternal connections and possible expressions of grief within these majestic creatures.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/heartbreaking-and-extremely-rare-mother-humpback-whale-carries-stillborn-calf-through-the-ocean-scientists-explain-the-unusual-behaviour/articleshow/134326041.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/heartbreaking-and-extremely-rare-mother-humpback-whale-carries-stillborn-calf-through-the-ocean-scientists-explain-the-unusual-behaviour/articleshow/134326041.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T11:22:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134326091,imgsize-826691.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California homeowner’s $5,000 pool faces removal 53 years later in sewer easement dispute]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134310203.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In Huntington Beach, 29 homeowners are in a legal dispute with the Orange County Sanitation District over a 30-foot sewer easement running through their backyards. Some residents had built pools and other structures with city permits. OC San says the space is needed to maintain an ageing wastewater pipeline, while a court has allowed the homeowners’ case to proceed to trial.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1973-a-california-homeowner-paid-5000-for-a-city-permitted-backyard-pool-53-years-later-a-sanitation-district-says-it-must-go-as-the-29-property-easement-dispute-heads-to-trial/articleshow/134310203.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1973-a-california-homeowner-paid-5000-for-a-city-permitted-backyard-pool-53-years-later-a-sanitation-district-says-it-must-go-as-the-29-property-easement-dispute-heads-to-trial/articleshow/134310203.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T11:03:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134310622,imgsize-302400.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Venomous sea snake returns to California beach after 8 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134326779.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/yellow-bellied-venomous-sea-snake-returns-to-california-beach-after-8-years-rare-reappearance-after-2018-gives-scientists-clues-about-the-species-changing-pacific-range/articleshow/134326779.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/yellow-bellied-venomous-sea-snake-returns-to-california-beach-after-8-years-rare-reappearance-after-2018-gives-scientists-clues-about-the-species-changing-pacific-range/articleshow/134326779.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T10:59:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134326847,imgsize-235449.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ohio Park Set To Expand: Homestead Metro Park to add 333 acres; new trails, habitats planned]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134310209.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Homestead Metro Park in Hilliard, Ohio, is set to bloom with an expansive addition of 333 conservation acres, elevating its size to nearly nine times larger than before. This remarkable land transfer is a collaboration between the city and M/I Homes, paving the way for enhanced trails and natural habitats. Visitors can look forward to exploring this enlarged haven after several years of dedicated development.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-ohio-park-covered-just-43-acres-a-land-transfer-involving-the-city-and-a-h