Iran.  Iran's Revolutionary Guard controls the Strait of Hormuz, restricting vessel passage.  The US military maintains a naval blockade on Iranian ports.  Recent tanker incidents raise concerns about regional stability and oil flow.  Trump will meet Gulf leaders to discuss the conflict's next phase.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/do-i-want-to-annihilate-them-trump-weighs-next-phase-of-iran-war/articleshow/134323883.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/do-i-want-to-annihilate-them-trump-weighs-next-phase-of-iran-war/articleshow/134323883.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T07:40:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134323929,imgsize-59618.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Owens Questions School Event: Candace Owens alleges TPUSA forced assembly; online fight over youth outreach]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134323132.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Candace Owens questioned a TPUSA Club America event at Nampa Christian School after images showed more than 500 high school students gathered in the gym. Owens claimed students were required to attend and that parents were not allowed to join them. A separate post celebrated the turnout and Erika Kirk’s appearance. The claims sparked online debate over political outreach in schools and student participation, with details about attendance policies remaining disputed.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/forcing-events-on-underage-kids-candace-owens-calls-out-erika-kirk-and-tpusa-school-event-after-500-plus-students-reportedly-attend-nampa-gathering/articleshow/134323132.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/forcing-events-on-underage-kids-candace-owens-calls-out-erika-kirk-and-tpusa-school-event-after-500-plus-students-reportedly-attend-nampa-gathering/articleshow/134323132.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T05:52:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134323172,imgsize-1006854.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[TikToker Killing Probed: Evelyn Lima Dantas shot dead after release; retaliation eyed]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134323125.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Brazilian TikToker Evelyn Lima Dantas, 21, was reportedly shot and killed in Mãe do Rio, Brazil, on Sept. 16. Police said two men allegedly entered her home, dragged her outside and shot her multiple times. Dantas had more than 150,000 followers across social media. She had been arrested in July during an investigation into a police sergeant’s killing and was provisionally released on Sept. 9. Authorities are investigating a possible connection.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/what-happened-to-evelyn-lima-dantas-brazilian-tiktoker-shot-and-killed-at-21/articleshow/134323125.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/what-happened-to-evelyn-lima-dantas-brazilian-tiktoker-shot-and-killed-at-21/articleshow/134323125.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-18T05:31:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134323128,imgsize-68080.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australia cracks down on student and backpacker visas to curb migration]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://tim